.TH "INSPEKT\-AXE" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-axe \- Run axe\-core accessibility audit on the current page.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]axe\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run axe\-core accessibility audit on the current page.
.PP
Analyzes the page for WCAG conformance violations using the
industry\-standard axe\-core library.
By default, tests against WCAG 2 Level AA standards.
.PP
The audit runs in the current browser tab, testing the actual rendered
page state including any JavaScript\-generated content and
authentication state.
.PP
Supported WCAG levels:
.IP \(bu 2
2a: WCAG 2.0 Level A
.IP \(bu 2
2aa: WCAG 2.0 Level AA (default)
.IP \(bu 2
2aaa: WCAG 2.0 Level AAA
.IP \(bu 2
21a: WCAG 2.1 Level A
.IP \(bu 2
21aa: WCAG 2.1 Level AA
.IP \(bu 2
22aa: WCAG 2.2 Level AA
.PP
Additional tags like `best\-practice' or `experimental' can be included.
.SH ALIASES
Also available as: \f[B]inspekt a11y\f[R], \f[B]inspekt
accessibility\f[R].
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enlevel\f[R], \f[I][2a|2aa|2aaa|21a|21aa|22aa]\f[R]
WCAG conformance level to test (default: 2aa)
.TP
\f[B]\(enrule\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Check specific accessibility rule by ID (e.g., `color\-contrast',
`link\-name')
.TP
\f[B]\(enlist\-rules\f[R]
List all available axe\-core rules and exit
.TP
\f[B]\(entags\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Additional comma\-separated tags (e.g., `best\-practice,experimental')
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-passes\f[R]
Include passing checks in output
.TP
\f[B]\(eninclude\-incomplete\f[R]
Include incomplete checks (require manual review)
.TP
\f[B]\(enjson\f[R]
Output full results as JSON
.TP
\f[B]\(entimeout\f[R], \f[I]FLOAT\f[R]
Timeout in seconds (default: 30)
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-select\f[R]
Disable auto\-selection of element when single violation is found (only
applies to \(enrule checks)
.TP
\f[B]\(enscoped\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Scope tests to specific elements.
Use `inspected' for the currently inspected element, or provide CSS
selectors (comma\-separated)
.TP
\f[B]\(enexclude\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
Exclude elements from testing.
Can be comma\-separated selectors or multiple \(enexclude flags
(repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enrequire\-panel\-selection\f[R]
Require element to be selected via Inspekt panel (not DevTools).
Only valid with \(enscoped inspected
.TP
\f[B]\(enshow\-badges\f[R]
Show numbered severity badges on violating elements (default: from
config)
.TP
\f[B]\(eninteractive\f[R]
Make badges clickable with detailed popover information (requires
\(enshow\-badges)
.TP
\f[B]\(endev\-css\f[R]
Load CSS from local server (http://localhost:5500) for live editing.
Use with VS Code Live Server.
.TP
\f[B]\(enpersistent\f[R]
Monitor and re\-run audit on each page navigation (press Ctrl+C to
stop).
CLI only.
.TP
\f[B]\(endisable\-rule\f[R], \f[I]RULE_ID\f[R]
Disable specific rules by ID.
Supports comma\-separated values.
(repeatable)
.TP
\f[B]\(enenable\-rule\f[R], \f[I]RULE_ID\f[R]
Run ONLY these rules (all others disabled).
Supports comma\-separated values.
(repeatable)
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt axe
inspekt axe \-\-level 21aa
inspekt axe \-\-level 22aa \-\-tags best\-practice
inspekt axe \-\-include\-passes \-\-include\-incomplete
inspekt axe \-\-rule color\-contrast
.EE
